perf(pip): Rate govern the diagnostics we keep on, so a long session does not fill the log

The probes that read render targets back are already off by default; this is about the lines that
stayed on, which added up over hours.

 - the per optic line fired whenever the lens FOV changed, and a dynamic zoom sight changes it on
   every frame of its zoom animation, so raising a variable power optic cost ten to twenty lines per
   aim. It is now a summary written once when the aim ends (plus a five minute heartbeat for a held
   aim), reporting the optic, the range of lens FOV and power that the aim covered - which is what
   those per step lines were read for - together with the current facts. Nothing is written while
   the values simply keep moving.
 - the state line ran every 300 frames while an optic was up: 720 lines per hour with nothing new to
   say. It now writes on a change of lens/target state plus the same five minute heartbeat.
 - the thermal optic line and the "second target set is missing" warning likewise write once per
   episode instead of on a timer.
 - the per pass line (debug only) is throttled to every 600 frames instead of 120.
 - the state leak warning fires every frame while leaking; it is now reported once per session.

What stays as it was: the one off messages (target set created, pack policy, build stamp), which are
per session and worth having.